# SprintBias command registry — THE source of truth for the command catalog.
#
# Every user-facing command has exactly one row here. The runtime index
# (./sprint.sh help) is GENERATED from this file, and ./sprint.sh validate
# --commands enforces that the dispatch table, the help/*.md pages, and
# DOCUMENTATION.md all match it. Add a command = add a row here + a help page;
# the index updates itself and the validator guards the rest.
#
# Format (pipe-delimited, 4 fields + optional 5th):
#   command | group | usage-suffix | one-line summary | demo-name
# group is one of: create | chat | plan | work | look | keep
# usage-suffix is the arg hint shown after the command (may be empty).
# demo-name (OPTIONAL 5th field) maps this command to a shipped demo under
#   learning/<demo-name>.py. When set, `./sprint.sh <cmd> --demo` plays it and
#   `<cmd> --help` gains a "Demo:  ./sprint.sh <cmd> --demo" pointer. Leave it
#   empty (or omit the 5th field entirely) for no demo — the default. Story
#   tasks populate this for their own host command; do not invent a second
#   command→demo mapping scheme elsewhere.
# Lines starting with # and blank lines are ignored. Order within a group is
# display order. A command may have a second row for a notable sub-form
# (e.g. validate --docs); existence checks dedupe on the command field.

newidea       | create   | [name]              | Create a new idea (no name = AI Q&A) | newidea
newfeature    | create   | [name]              | Create a new feature (no name = AI Q&A) | newfeature
newtask       | create   | <description>       | Create a new task | newtask
newplan       | create   | <name> [task-id...|parent:N] | Create a plan — named task-ID list; parent:N binds open parent+children (fast lane) | newplan
newbug        | create   | <description>       | Report a new bug | bug
newtest       | create   | <name>              | Create a test loop to validate a deployed thing | newtest

chat          | chat     | [target]            | id: define/refine/split one task · folder (blocked/next/backlog): sweep · plan [id]: author a plan · bugs: sweep inbox · nothing: walk sprint health (spine: chat → plan start → work) | chat

plan          | plan     | think/start/done [id] | think: dual-persona plan critique · start: gate + commit members to next/ (the sprint), latches STARTED · done: delete the plan once every member is in done/ — heads the spine → work | feature-plan

work          | work     | [N] [count N] [--fast] | Execute — happy path: run READY tasks in next/ → review/ (after plan start). `work N` works one task by id; `count N` caps how many run | work
loop          | work     | [--refill] [--retry]| Autopilot spine — plan start refill (gates as it commits) then work drain | loop
gate          | work     | [folder] [limit]    | Off-spine quality gate — re-gate next/ (--force) or report on backlog/doing/blocked (not the happy path) | gate
settle        | work     | [id] [--dry-run] [--blocked] | Accept (Suggestion: …) open questions — fold into Notes, clear list; demote next/ files that still need a human
split         | work     | <path>              | Off-spine — one-shot split of a large task into subtasks (no conversation) | split
polish        | work     | [limit/id/file] [--code] [--rounds N] | After work — quality sweep review/, deep-judge a task (by id or file), or --code audit | polish
promote       | work     | [id] [--dry-run]    | Test-gated close — run each review/ task's **Tests**, all green → done/ | promote

status        | look     |                     | Show project status | status
search        | look     | <keyword>           | Search tasks by keyword | search
learn         | look     | [demo]              | Watch the flow run — play a sandboxed demo (no name = list demos) | learn
align         | look     |                     | Analyze feature alignment | align
context       | look     |                     | Generate AI context summary | context

profile       | keep     |                     | Create or update project profile (interactive) | profile
profile       | keep     | show                | Print current project profile (no AI)
sync          | keep     | [--all]             | Push task changes to GitHub | sync
validate      | keep     | [--fix] [--dry-run] | Integrity-check task IDs and Depends on / Dependents | validate
validate      | keep     | --docs              | Check help/*.md for flag drift vs scripts
validate      | keep     | --commands          | Check every command is fully surfaced (this registry ↔ dispatch ↔ help ↔ manual)
cleanup       | keep     | [--delete/--force/--all] | Clean stale scratch files | cleanup
deps          | keep     |                     | File a backlog task auditing outdated/vulnerable deps | deps
model         | keep     | show/list/set [k v] | See the effective AI model per role, list provider models, or set a default (no AI)
config        | keep     |                     | Interactively set the AI provider and default model in docs/sprintbias/config (no AI)
